translations.text:
सद्दर्शनं (saddarśanaṁ)
 – true vision; 
द्राविडवाङ्निबद्धं (drāviḍavāṅnibaddhaṁ)
 – composed in Dravida language (द्राविड:Dravida | वाङ्:language | निबद्धं:composed); 
महर्षिणा (maharṣiṇā)
 – by the great sage; 
श्रीरमणेन (śrīramaṇena)
 – by Sri Ramana; 
शुद्धम् (śuddham)
 – pure; 
प्रबन्धमुत्कृष्टममर्त्यवाण्या (prabandhamutkṛṣṭamamartyavāṇyā)
 – composition excellent in immortals’ language (प्रबन्धम्:composition | उत्कृष्टम्:excellent | अमर्त्यवाण्या:in immortals’ language); 
मनूद्य (manūdya)
 – spoken afterward; 
वासिष्ठमुनिर्व्यतानीत् (vāsiṣṭhamunirvyatānīt)
 – Vasishta Muni composed (वासिष्ठ:Vasishta | मुनिः:sage | व्यतानीत्:composed);

सत्तत्त्वसारं (sattattvasāraṁ)
 – essence of truth (सत्:truth | तत्त्व:principle | सारं:essence); 
सरलं (saralaṁ)
 – straight-forwardly; 
दधाना (dadhānā)
 – giving; 
मुमुक्षुलोकाय (mumukṣulokāya)
 – to seekers of liberation (मुमुक्षु:seeker of liberation | लोकाय:to the world); 
मुदं (mudaṁ)
 – joy; 
ददाना (dadānā)
 – giving; 
अमानुषश्रीरमणीयवाणी- (amānuṣaśrīramaṇīyavāṇī-)
 – divine Ramana's delightful voice (अमानुष:divine | श्रीरमणीय:Sri Ramana's delightful | वाणी:voice); 
मयूखभित्तिर्मुनिवाग् (mayūkhabhittirmunivāg)
 – rays of light, Muni's speech (मयूख:rays of light | भित्तिः:wall-like surface | मुनिवाग्:Muni's speech); 
विभाति (vibhāti)
 – shines;
